UnitCappedTokenTransfersHub::constructor
├── When called
│   ├── it sets the safe
│   ├── it sets the recipient
│   ├── it sets the epoch length
│   └── it sets the tokens and caps
├── When tokens registered contain a duplicated token
│   └── it reverts
├── When the epoch length is zero
│   └── it reverts
├── When the tokens and caps length mismatch
│   └── it reverts
└── When the cap is zero
    └── it reverts

UnitCappedTokenTransfersHub::createNewActionsBuilder
├── When called by the safe owner
│   ├── When the token is not registered in the hub
│   │   └── it reverts
│   └── When the token is registered in the hub
│       ├── it creates a new CappedTokenTransfers actions builder
│       ├── it sets the hub address in the child contract
│       └── it emits the event CappedTokenTransfersCreated
└── When not called by the safe owner
    └── It reverts

UnitCappedTokenTransfersHub::updateState
├── When called by the safe
│   ├── when the current epoch is greater than the epoch of the state
│   │   ├── it resets the total spent
│   │   └── it updates the last epoch
│   ├── it increments the total spent
│   ├── it emits the StateUpdated event
│   └── when the total spent is greater than the cap
│       └── it reverts
└── When not called by the safe
    └── It reverts

UnitCappedTokenTransfersHub::tokens
└── When called
    └── it returns the tokens

UnitCappedTokenTransfersHub::capLeft
├── When token does not exist
│   └── it returns zero
└── When token exists
    ├── when the current epoch is greater than the epoch of the state
    │   └── it returns the full cap
    └── when the current epoch is the same as the epoch of the state
        └── it returns the cap left for the token
